{
  "description": "A scan of an L bracket built back as Reconstruct built it (each plane tilted a few millionths of a radian by the scan): the L extruded, then each plate extruded again with its hole of radius 4 in its profile, joined (the L already holds the plates, so the joins leave slivers under 0.001 mm thick, one with the start of the radius 4 bore), then a hole of radius 3.9991 cut through the upright 0.004 mm off that bore. The cut leaves a crescent of face 0.04 mm2 between the two circles. SolidCraft's export once read its loop's turn from a polygon through 33 points of each edge, got it backwards, and wrote the face facing into the material: the body passed as made and the next boolean on it was refused.",
